  "tier": "told-once",
  "plain": "In the 1960s Andrija Puharich, a doctor and inventor who also studied telepathy, invented a device called the TD-100, short for \"Transdermal 100,\" meaning it worked through the skin, at a company called Intelectron, and then it went out of sight. A researcher named Greg Malatzi tells Michels this without naming a source. He tells it as part of a story about the CIA's interest in Puharich's work, where a device vanishing would hint at secret use."
